WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.140
Before we start knitting, let's find the
first row of the punch card

2
00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:10.780
with no yarn or stitches, put 24 needles
in work in the middle of the machine.

3
00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:15.820
Start with the card inserted
so the first row is showing.

4
00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:20.020
Manually rotate the card down 7 rows.

5
00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:21.940
Lock the card.

6
00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:28.820
This should align the card to the first
row of holes down inside that card reader.

7
00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:31.100
Test the alignment of the card by passing

8
00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:34.460
the carriage over the
empty needles in work.

9
00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:40.120
The needles corresponding to the first
row of holes should be selected.

10
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:44.920
Now we need to get some stitches
on the needles in the ribber.

11
00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.500
Caston for full needle rib.

12
00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:52.480
Knit a zig-zag row.

13
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.380
Because we're going to
be dropping stitches.

14
00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:09.280
It's critical that we hang
the cast on comb correctly.

15
00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:17.050
With the zigzag row and
the cast on comb in place,

16
00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:22.540
Use the D-slider and drop all the main bed
stitches and make sure they are all

17
00:01:22.570 --> 00:01:28.290
aligned to B position
and remove the D-slider.

18
00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:31.570
This technique also needs more weight.

19
00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:35.490
You'll need to experiment with your yarn.

20
00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:39.140
Your carriage and your
working yarn are on the left.

21
00:01:39.170 --> 00:01:42.740
All of the main bed
needles are in B position.

22
00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:47.280
Press in both part
buttons on the main bed.

23
00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:54.960
Knit one row to the right
across the ribber needles only.

24
00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:59.020
Set your change knob to KC.

25
00:01:59.050 --> 00:02:06.560
Align that punch card to the first row
of the pattern and knit to the left.

26
00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:08.080
The ribber stitches.

27
00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:13.780
Knit needles are selected on the main
bed. Knit to the right, the ribber

28
00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:19.560
stitches continue to knit and there
are loops on the main bed needles.

29
00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:22.220
With the carriage on the right,

30
00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:26.500
Use that D-slider and drop the loops.

31
00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:30.220
Remember, the D-slider only
goes in one direction.

32
00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:34.140
Pull down on the knitting to get
those loose loops out of the way.

33
00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:36.260
Keep repeating this sequence.

34
00:02:36.290 --> 00:02:40.300
Knit left and the needles on
the main bed are selected.

35
00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:44.220
Knit right loops are formed and all the

36
00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:47.700
while the knitting is
happening on the ribber.

37
00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:54.660
Use the D-slider to drop the loops
or you can just manually drop them.

38
00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:57.540
Continue to repeat this sequence.

39
00:02:57.570 --> 00:03:00.000
Knit to the left and the needles are

40
00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:06.060
selected on the main bed, knit to
the right and loops are formed.

41
00:03:06.090 --> 00:03:08.740
Drop those loops.

42
00:03:08.770 --> 00:03:14.100
Drop stitch lace is an amazing technique
that you need to try for yourself.

43
00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:16.980
Don't get overwhelmed by all the steps.

44
00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:22.520
Take it one step at a time and you'll be
knitting lace on your bulky in no time.

